   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 431 of the laws of 2018 relating to authorizing the\nstate commissioner of transportation to convey real property to the town of\nHuntington, county of Suffolk, in relation to extending certain provisions",
    "basePrintNo": "S5819",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5819-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§4 & 5, Chap 431 of 2018",
    "lawSection": "Suffolk County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5819\n\nSPONSOR: MATTERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 431 of the laws of 2018 relating to authorizing\nthe state commissioner of transportation to convey real property to the\ntown of Huntington, county of Suffolk, in relation to extending certain\nprovisions\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nExtends by one year the date in which the property referenced in chapter\n431 of the laws of 2018 may be transferred to the town of Huntington by\nthe state commissioner of transportation.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: amends Sections 4 and 5 of chapter 431 of the laws of 2018.\n\nSection 2: sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 431 of the Laws of 2018 authorized the conveyance, within 5\nyears, of 4.2 acres of real property from the State Department of Trans-\nportation (DOT) to the Town of Huntington for use in a major economic\ndevelopment project in the hamlet of Huntington Station.\n\nThe Huntington Station area is undergoing a transformative mixed-use\nrevitalization, under the auspices of a Public-Private Partnership\nbetween the Town of Huntington and its Master Developer, Renaissance\nDowntowns. This partnership has conducted significant public outreach\nand economic research on the project. As DOT controls a portion of the\nland needed to complete the project, the Department has been working\nclosely with Huntington officials to transfer the necessary parcels to\nthe Town. This legislation is the byproduct of those negotiations, which\nare still ongoing, and will extend by one year the date in which the\nsubject property may be transferred to the town of Huntington by the\nstate commissioner of transportation.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
